A||N||19||Voytek||Shipping With UPS - IT SUCKS!!!!!||||8||
Z||000000||Voytek||11-15-2001||02:49 PM||||Ok, here is my gripe.  And yes, it's somewhat Fiero related since the stuff was shipped to me from the Fiero Store.<P>I ordered a set of poly bushings for my '87 GT.  It was sent out UPS, $18.00 USD ($29 CDN) for REGULAR ground shipping. Fine.  So the package gets here and the leave a note on my door yesterday.  The note says $59 CDN bucks in brokerage!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> WHAT TH' HELL??  So I call the place and find out that, since they're not a 'bonded' courier (whatever th' f***k that means) they have to charge me local taxes.<P>FINE.  I want my stuff.  So I tell them I work every day and therefore am not at home (duh).  Guess what?  UPS will attempt to deliver the package for 3 days in a row.  If they're not successful, the package will be sent BACK to the Fiero Store on the 3rd day !!!(??) <P>So I ask for the phone number of the local depot so I can pick it up.  'Sorry sir, we can't give you this information as they do not answer any calls'.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  to which I answer: 'so the driver will be DRIVING around TOWN for the next 3 DAYS with this package, and I CAN'T PICK IT UP?????<BR>'No sir'.<P>So now I need to make special arrangements in order for them to hold the package on Monday so I can pick it up or else it will go back to the Fiero Store.<P>Let me get this straight.  A $215 CDN order is going to cost me an additional $88 BUCKS to get through UPS!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>As a comparison, the Sprint headers I ordered were valued at $850 CDN.  Sent with the postal service (one week, just like UPS), I paid about $30 bucks in brokerage and no tax.<P>Has anyone heard of NAFTA?????!!!!<P>I don't know about shipping within the USA but if you, Canadians want to avoid hassles when ordering from the US, USE THE POSTAL SERVICE!! (or FedEx - they're better than UPS).<P>The venting is complete.  No need to comment, just take my advice.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||8
Z||000001||Jaygee79||11-15-2001||03:37 PM||||Actually you could've had them redirect it to your work so you could receive it there.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Voytek||11-15-2001||03:43 PM||||Well, the good lady at the end of the line didn't give me that option when I told her that I work and I am never at home.<P>Another reason for me not to use them again.<P>Bitter?  Yes, I am.||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroMontreal||11-15-2001||04:16 PM||||I made a trade for some parts with a fellow list member. He shipped the items useing UPS. When I got the Item I had to pay $61.00!!! I didn't pay anything for the parts since it was a trade but because the guy I traded with put the value of the items as $98.00 they charged ne taxes! I do not blame the list member, it was not his fault. UPS sucks and I never want to use them again.. USPS all the way!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigfieromontreal_1.gif">  <BR>1986 Fiero GT, STOCK Wingless, <BR>-Alex President of FieroMontreal... <A HREF="http://www.fieromontreal.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieromontreal.com</A> <BR>and Regional Director of CFOG-I for Eastern Canada.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fiero_24||11-15-2001||04:21 PM||||UPS does suck!  I had a package from the Fiero Store sent second day air to 1200 Claremont, and it went to 1250 Morse Ave.  I had it 2nd day air, but got it 6 days later due to their dumb A$$ faults.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/driverside41.jpg"> <BR>  <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT||||reg||8
Z||000005||Brandon86SE||11-15-2001||04:31 PM||||Voytek - You could get them shipped here.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I'm home.  (no promises you'll ever see them though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">)<P>Brandon||||reg||1
Z||000006||Voytek||11-15-2001||05:08 PM||||He he he, that's a great idea Brandon!  why didn't I think of that SOONER?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Glad to see that I'm not the only dissatisfied 'former' customer.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Mickey_Moose||11-15-2001||05:49 PM||||a couple of things here...<P>you can tell them to hold the package at their distrubution center and you will pick it up there.<P>find out where it came into Canada from? If it came in through customs in Calgary you can tell UPS to shove it and send it back to Customs Canada (assuming it came to customs in Calgary) and you will go there yourself and clear the package. You will just have to pay the usual taxes, but no stupid brokerage fee. There is some paper work involved (I forget what there all was to do - but you can call customs and find out - there was not too much to do). UPS can tell you where it came into Canada.<P>I have had this problem before  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">, unfortunatly it's too far for me to drive to the custom office  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Anyone else in Canada getting parts in from the US, always ship via the Postal Service, that way you will only pay GST.<P>Tim<BR>||||reg||4
Z||000008||Voytek||11-15-2001||06:03 PM||||First off, yeah, you can tell them to hold it there, BUT, not until the delivery boy makes 3 tries at my home.  Figure that one out.  THEN you don't have a very long window before they send it back to the originator if you don't claim the package.  Now, I WANTED to claim the packgae but they wouldn't even give me the phone # to the distribution center because, apparently, no one answers the phone there.  Whatever.<P>I will find out about the customs thing, though.  Thanks for the suggestion.  I sure don't want to pay $44 bucks in brokerage fees(set by UPS).<P>I just checked.  The package cleared through Winnipeg.  No point driving 12 hours to save $44 bucks.<P>BTW Everyone: UPS sets the charge for filling out the forms for brokerage and you can't argue on the amount (I tried).  THEY are the ones that are ripping me off.<p>[This message has been edited by Voytek (edited 11-15-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||Back On Holiday||11-15-2001||09:02 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Voytek:<BR><B>First off, yeah, you can tell them to hold it there, BUT, not until the delivery boy makes 3 tries at my home.  Figure that one out.  THEN you don't have a very long window before they send it back to the originator if you don't claim the package.  Now, I WANTED to claim the packgae but they wouldn't even give me the phone # to the distribution center because, apparently, no one answers the phone there.  Whatever.<P>I will find out about the customs thing, though.  Thanks for the suggestion.  I sure don't want to pay $44 bucks in brokerage fees(set by UPS).<P>I just checked.  The package cleared through Winnipeg.  No point driving 12 hours to save $44 bucks.<P>BTW Everyone: UPS sets the charge for filling out the forms for brokerage and you can't argue on the amount (I tried).  THEY are the ones that are ripping me off.<P>[This message has been edited by Voytek (edited 11-15-2001).]</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Your Note should say :COD AMOUNT $xx.xx<P>Leave a check on the door made out to the UPS brokerage, UPS driver will leave package.<P>Andrew Lewis - UPS Driver||||reg||1
Z||000010||Custom84cp||11-15-2001||09:29 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Voytek:<BR><B>Ok, here is my gripe.  And yes, it's somewhat Fiero related since the stuff was shipped to me from the Fiero Store.<P>I ordered a set of poly bushings for my '87 GT.  It was sent out UPS, $18.00 USD ($29 CDN) for REGULAR ground shipping. Fine.  So the package gets here and the leave a note on my door yesterday.  The note says $59 CDN bucks in brokerage!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> WHAT TH' HELL??  So I call the place and find out that, since they're not a 'bonded' courier (whatever th' f***k that means) they have to charge me local taxes.<P>FINE.  I want my stuff.  So I tell them I work every day and therefore am not at home (duh).  Guess what?  UPS will attempt to deliver the package for 3 days in a row.  If they're not successful, the package will be sent BACK to the Fiero Store on the 3rd day !!!(??) <P>So I ask for the phone number of the local depot so I can pick it up.  'Sorry sir, we can't give you this information as they do not answer any calls'.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  to which I answer: 'so the driver will be DRIVING around TOWN for the next 3 DAYS with this package, and I CAN'T PICK IT UP?????<BR>'No sir'.<P>So now I need to make special arrangements in order for them to hold the package on Monday so I can pick it up or else it will go back to the Fiero Store.<P>Let me get this straight.  A $215 CDN order is going to cost me an additional $88 BUCKS to get through UPS!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>As a comparison, the Sprint headers I ordered were valued at $850 CDN.  Sent with the postal service (one week, just like UPS), I paid about $30 bucks in brokerage and no tax.<P>Has anyone heard of NAFTA?????!!!!<P>I don't know about shipping within the USA but if you, Canadians want to avoid hassles when ordering from the US, USE THE POSTAL SERVICE!! (or FedEx - they're better than UPS).<P>The venting is complete.  No need to comment, just take my advice.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>If you knew you wern't going to be home then why did you have the package sent there? Have it sent to your work! If you find your local UPS driver he will be glad to give you your package. And, you can call and have the package put in will call(held at the center) for 7 days after the first 3 atemps. And, I beleive that it is YOUR goverment that set's the International tax rate you are being charged, NOT UPS! And, FedEx proceses 3 Mil packages a day, UPS does 13 Mil, give them a break!!!<P>||||reg||1
Z||000011||72vinman||11-15-2001||10:39 PM||||I sympathize. I had the exact same problem with them. Brokerage fees my a**. I will never use them again.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigvin2_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Adrift||11-15-2001||11:06 PM||||Check this out: <A HREF="http://homepage.mac.com/simonster/PhotoAlbum3.html" TARGET=_blank>http://homepage.mac.com/simonster/PhotoAlbum3.html</A> <P>You'll never ship UPS again||||reg||1
Z||000013||jelly2m8||11-15-2001||11:09 PM||||Ya, using UPS sux on this end of the border.<P>UPS gets it through customs, an stuff faster, but you pay thru the nose for it!.<P>You can also thank our government for the duty fees and tax that they slip in there.<P>I try to use plain old mail, its slower but cheaper.||||reg||1
Z||000014||Hank is Here||11-15-2001||11:23 PM||||I think NAFTA is only for products in the North America.  Are the poly bushings made in the USA or abroab?  Also I think I heard one time that there are no taxes for auto parts across the boarder.  Even though UPS did clear the package through customs.   <P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Voytek:<BR><B><BR>Has anyone heard of NAFTA?????!!!!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000015||Adrift||11-16-2001||12:44 AM||||There's no added duties, but there are taxes (%15 in ontario). The truth is though that there is a flat $5 added duty fee, if sent USPS (On autoparts only... on computer parts, for example, there are higher duty fees)||||reg||1
Z||000016||Jaygee79||11-16-2001||01:00 AM||||None of the damage in the pics there would have happened if it had been packed properly.  You can tell just by looking at it that whoever packed it didn't do it right.||||reg||1
Z||000017||Voytek||11-16-2001||10:25 AM||||Custom84cp: <B>ACTUALLY</B> it IS the UPS that sets the brokerage rate - in this case all $44 bucks of it.  It is the cost for them to fill out a form for me.  BFD!!!  I could fill out a form within a few minutes and get the package for free through customs!<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>If you knew you wern't going to be home then why did you have the package sent there?<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>FYI: The post office leaves a notice on the door and I can pick up the package from the storage.  FedEx has done the same for me in the past.  Maybe I should have asked you for advice before I shipped the package.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>BTW, the post office does NOT charge this ridiculous amount.  I paid about 30 bucks on an $850 CDN order.<P>Back On Holiday - good suggestion but would YOU want to have a package worth almost $300 bucks (including fees) sitting in front of your door the whole day?  I don't exactly live in an 'upscale' neighborhood.  People take stuff just for kicks these days, even if it's got little or no use to them.||||reg||1
Z||000018||Mickey_Moose||11-16-2001||06:29 PM||||hmmm, that's odd...the last time I used UPS (never again - also), I called them and told them to leave it at the pickup counter (this after 1st attempt) and I picked it up the next day - sounds like you are getting a rookie on the phone.<P>Tim<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000019||Back On Holiday||11-17-2001||12:46 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Voytek:<BR><B>Custom84cp: [b]ACTUALLY</B> it IS the UPS that sets the brokerage rate - in this case all $44 bucks of it.  It is the cost for them to fill out a form for me.  BFD!!!  I could fill out a form within a few minutes and get the package for free through customs!<P> FYI: The post office leaves a notice on the door and I can pick up the package from the storage.  FedEx has done the same for me in the past.  Maybe I should have asked you for advice before I shipped the package.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>BTW, the post office does NOT charge this ridiculous amount.  I paid about 30 bucks on an $850 CDN order.<P>Back On Holiday - good suggestion but would YOU want to have a package worth almost $300 bucks (including fees) sitting in front of your door the whole day?  I don't exactly live in an 'upscale' neighborhood.  People take stuff just for kicks these days, even if it's got little or no use to them.[/B]<HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>To Voytek: didn't realize you were in that situation, maybe a neigbor you can trust?<P>To, Jaygee79  -Your right.  I've seen that packaging material, my child can rip it with his pinky.  As for the computer being damaged, that guy must have been cheap not to pack it properly, that's why ALL the computer companies ship with HUGE wads of Styrofoam inserts to protect their merchandise.  The Facility I work in has a normal input of 70,000 packages per day, now its starting to range around 100,000<BR>out of that 100k, I delivered approx 400 packages today and none were damaged.<BR>if your stuff is important, pack it properly.<P>As for the Int'l Fees, theres a ton of diffrent options that are legal or not legal.<BR>i've seen people have it sent to a friends house in Maine and picked up and taken back across the border.<BR>Andrew Lewis<P>------------------<BR>84se Silver 2m4<BR>86se Silver 2m6||||reg||1
